{"status":"completed","summary":"Created `Fleet Internal CA` on node1, issued a certificate for node2, and configured node2 to serve trusted HTTPS at https://10.100.129.11:8443/. The CA is trusted system-wide on both nodes. Both nodes were restarted sequentially and fully recovered with changed boot identities, unchanged OS release/kernel, and persistent TLS functionality.","actions_performed":["Installed the signed RHEL OpenSSL tooling only on node1.","Created the CA with a protected 4096-bit private key and critical CA constraints.","Generated node2’s 3072-bit TLS private key locally on node2 and issued a server-auth certificate containing DNS and IP SANs.","Installed the CA in both RHEL system trust stores.","Created an enabled, hardened systemd HTTPS service running under a locked dedicated account on node2.","Opened only TCP/8443 in node2’s runtime and persistent firewalld configuration.","Verified successful trusted HTTPS, TLS-only behavior, and rejection of an incorrect hostname.","Removed temporary transfer artifacts and audited listeners, permissions, failed units, administrative access, release, and kernel state.","Restarted node1 and node2 one at a time and verified changed boot identities plus complete recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Create Fleet Internal CA on node1","command_ids":["cmd-7f7ea1b2795b4c47","cmd-e9a427d2ec834f36"],"summary":"Shows the self-signed `CN=Fleet Internal CA`, critical CA constraints/key usage, fingerprint, protected key permissions, and durable CA files."},{"requirement":"Issue a valid TLS certificate for node2","command_ids":["cmd-6fef42efaf914f9c","cmd-4f8ad70bc7e846af"],"summary":"Node2 generated its key locally; the issued non-CA certificate chains to Fleet Internal CA, has server-auth usage, and includes `DNS:node2` and `IP:10.100.129.11` SANs."},{"requirement":"Install the CA as a trusted system authority on both nodes","command_ids":["cmd-5fb307649d9d461f","cmd-6bfa0c523347477b","cmd-124aa1d205534876","cmd-a52768d894d54259"],"summary":"Node1’s system bundle verifies the chain, and default-trust curl requests on both nodes return HTTP 200 with `ssl_verify_result=0`, including after restart."},{"requirement":"Serve HTTPS on node2 port 8443 securely and persistently","command_ids":["cmd-24dc370e4fba4a60","cmd-76a0aa23095f4b94","cmd-68e8786628204f1b","cmd-82c0a77e85c440e8"],"summary":"The hardened service runs as `fleet-https`, listens at 10.100.129.11:8443, and has a persistent firewall allowance. TLS 1.3 peer verification succeeds; an incorrect hostname is rejected."},{"requirement":"Preserve installed OS release, kernel, administrative access, and security controls","command_ids":["cmd-be9662066c2346ef","cmd-846384234ef84f71","cmd-eb8b67b7dcf34ac6","cmd-23ec3538725d4aca"],"summary":"Before/after evidence shows RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 unchanged, SSH active, SELinux retained, expected listeners only, and no failed units or temporary residue."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-e9a427d2ec834f36","cmd-a1c213677ffa4399","cmd-2fb757c361d2475e","cmd-1470212a893b4168"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot identity, running system state, unchanged CA data, restored SSH/trust, and successful HTTPS access."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node2 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-f451b63e93b8409d","cmd-df6e494ceb4e4ae3","cmd-2961515729e448fb","cmd-a52768d894d54259","cmd-82c0a77e85c440e8"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered enabled service/listener/firewall, unchanged TLS material, and successful local and remote trusted HTTPS."}]}
